  "title": "Histograms and stem-and-leaf plots",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "Organising lots of numbers",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A long list of numbers is hard to read. We need to organise it.",
          "write": "organise the data"
        },
        {
          "say": "Think of pigeonholes in a school office. Each number goes in a hole.",
          "write": "class intervals"
        },
        {
          "say": "Then you can see straight away which hole is the fullest.",
          "write": "frequency"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Class intervals",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Group the values into classes of equal width, like 0 to less than 10.",
          "write": "0 to <10, 10 to <20, …"
        },
        {
          "say": "Here the class width is 10.",
          "write": "class width = 10"
        },
        {
          "say": "A value on a boundary, like 20, goes in the class that starts at 20.",
          "write": "20 → 20 to <30"
        },
        {
          "say": "Travel times of 24 students give frequencies 2, 7, 8, 5 and 2.",
          "write": "2 + 7 + 8 + 5 + 2 = 24 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
